{"type":"text","timestamp":1789150295735,"sessionID":"ses_f6e553ad4ffev0MfSUKDV7kkn9","part":{"id":"prt_091aaec340013bmWQxZt5IMjzM","sessionID":"ses_f6e553ad4ffev0MfSUKDV7kkn9","messageID":"msg_091aad6cb001o65eFx7awBGFye","type":"text","text":"### Proposed Plan: Book Tracker\n\nA lightweight, self-hosted web application for tracking your reading journey with persistent JSON storage and shareable book links.\n\n#### 1. Tech Stack\n- **Backend:** Node.js with Express (lightweight, zero-database, fast startup).\n- **Storage:** Local `books.json` file with atomic read/write operations for data persistence across restarts.\n- **Frontend:** Server-rendered HTML with semantic CSS and minimal vanilla JS for smooth interactions (e.g., one-click link copying).\n\n#### 2. Core Features & Interaction\n- **Home View (`/`):**\n  - Two distinct columns/sections: **Currently Reading** and **Finished**.\n  - Quick action on active books: **\"Mark as Finished\"** button.\n  - Quick-add form at the top (or expandable panel) to add a book with Title, Author, initial Notes, and starting status.\n- **Book Detail View (`/books/:id`):**\n  - Dedicated shareable URL for each book displaying title, author, reading status, and full notes.\n  - Includes a **\"Copy Link\"** helper button to quickly grab and share the URL.\n- **Data Persistence:** Automatically initializes and writes to `./data/books.json`.\n\n#### 3. Visual Design & UX\n- **Aesthetic:** Clean, modern editorial style with a warm paper-tone palette (soft cream background, deep charcoal typography, subtle border accents, and warm amber/sage status badges).\n- **Responsive:** Mobile-first layout that looks great on phones, tablets, and desktop displays.\n\n---\n\nDoes this plan look good to you, or would you like any adjustments before I begin implementation?","time":{"start":1789150295731,"end":1789150295731},"metadata":{"gateway":{"generationId":"gen_01M28TNNQEGEFKB1VRNWKCJYV9"}}}}
